Chapter: VM Profile

 The VM profile is a named bundle of code-generation knobs the compiler
 consults when emitting bare-metal infrastructure. The spec profile
 emits the canonical ATA bring-up; named profiles like QEMU-11.0.0
 select alternate sequences tuned to a specific emulator's behavior.

 Profile is selected via the compile mode protocol: "ELF" picks
 spec, "ELF QEMU-11.0.0" picks the QEMU profile.

Section: Profile Type
  VmProfile = record {
   name : Text,
   skip-ata-bring-up : Boolean
  }

Section: Built-in Profiles
  vm-profile-spec : VmProfile
  vm-profile-spec =
   VmProfile {
    name = "spec",
    skip-ata-bring-up = False
   }

  vm-profile-qemu-11-0-0 : VmProfile
  vm-profile-qemu-11-0-0 =
   VmProfile {
    name = "QEMU-11.0.0",
    skip-ata-bring-up = True
   }

Section: Lookup
  lookup-vm-profile : Text -> VmProfile
  lookup-vm-profile (name) =
   if name == "QEMU-11.0.0" then vm-profile-qemu-11-0-0
   else vm-profile-spec
